./skills/claude/yalla-dokploy-deploy/references/rollback.md:73:Caveats for git rollback:
./skills/claude/yalla-dokploy-deploy/references/rollback.md:74:- Dokploy must rebuild the image from the rolled-back source. Slower than image-tag rollback (which is just a `docker pull`).
./skills/claude/yalla-dokploy-deploy/references/rollback.md:76:- Schema migrations and rollback DON'T compose cleanly: if the broken version ran an irreversible migration, rolling back the code without rolling back the DB will fail at startup. See `migrations.md` § Anti-patterns.
./skills/claude/yalla-dokploy-deploy/references/rollback.md:78:## After rollback
