./skills/claude/yalla-dokploy-deploy/references/rollback.md:92:This way the **next** rollback knows to revert from v2.4.0 → v2.4.1 (the most recent prior), avoiding an undo loop where users accidentally re-roll-back to the broken version they just escaped from.
./skills/claude/yalla-dokploy-deploy/references/rollback.md:94:## When NOT to use rollback
./skills/claude/yalla-dokploy-deploy/references/rollback.md:100:- **You only need to stop traffic**: use `application-stop` (see `operations.md`), don't roll back. Rollback is for "the new version is broken AND the old version still works" — if the old version also can't run (DB schema changed), you don't have a rollback option.
