36-char length + server-side created_at + ExpiresAt round-trip + pending-side completion-consistent), Claim-respects-caller-supplied-id, Claim-duplicate-id-Conflict (PK collision on different (org, principal, key)), Claim-unknown-organization-Conflict (FK violation), Complete-row-shape (completed-side completion-consistent + created_at/expires_at non-drift), Complete-honours-explicit-now (specific 2024 timestamp), Complete-coerces-nil-body-to-empty (non-NULL empty bytea), Release-rejects-nil-tx, Release-on-completed-is-noop (row stays in place), Release-on-missing-key-is-noop, Claim-transaction-rollback (sentinel + countIdempotencyRowsForOrg == 0), Cascade-from-organization-delete (orgA wipe + orgB bystander byte-identity across id/route/request_hash/request_id/status/created_at/expires_at), Claim-peer-row-byte-identical, Find-returns-expired-row-as-is (Find does NOT filter on expires_at > now()), ExpiresAt-round-trip (microsecond-precise far-future timestamp). Note: idempotency_keys has NO updated_at column and NO BEFORE UPDATE trigger -- the peer-row byte-identity probe relies on the per-column projection across all 13 observable columns without a trigger-managed drift anchor (vs BE-0466 dokploy_refs which anchors on the set_updated_at trigger). Note: the response_status BETWEEN 100 AND 599 CHECK is unreachable from the typed Complete API (it pre-rejects out-of-range as apierr.Internal); same for the status IN ('pending', 'completed') CHECK (Claim hard-codes 'pending', Complete hard-codes 'completed'); same for the length() > 0 CHECKs on principal_id/idempotency_key/route/request_hash (Claim pre-validates these as apierr.InvalidInput). These CHECKs are pinned at the DB level only and NOT probed from Go in the invariants file -- the file header MUST document this delegation so a future reader does not mistake the absence for a coverage gap. New helpers introduced (per-file Idempotency-suffix to avoid store_test collisions): rawIdempotencyRow (with NULLABLE *int / *time.Time fields so pending NULLs are distinguishable from zero-value scalars), loadIdempotencyRowByID, countIdempotencyRowsForOrg, mintIdempotencyID, idempotencyTxRollbackSentinel. REUSED verbatim from sibling idempotency_test.go: idemFixture, claimIdem, completeIdem, findIdem, wantErrCode, newIdempotencyStore; from schema_test.go: seedOrg; from store_test.go: newStore. NO migration added. The byte-identical-bystander tenant-isolation gap-fill is the paired BE-0470 story. Forward-applicable to any future PRD CRUD-and-invariants story whose underlying table has a claim-protocol-style upsert on a non-PK UNIQUE tuple with a multi-column completion-consistent CHECK (e.g. a future webhook-delivery-claims or rate-limit-burst-tokens table).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000048-20260519-010141.log:987:- Repository CRUD-and-invariants tests for a **TABLE WHOSE SCHEMA ALREADY EXISTS FROM AN EARLY MIGRATION BUT WHOSE TYPED REPOSITORY IS THE FIRST STORY-LEVEL CALLER** -- i.e. the table landed in an ancient migration (dokploy_refs in 0002_tenant_hierarchy) and has been exercised only by raw-SQL schema_test.go tests; the CRUD-and-invariants PRD story creates BOTH the *_repository.go file AND the *_repository_invariants_test.go file from scratch (BE-0465 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/dokploy_ref.go + internal/controlplane/store/dokploy_ref_repository_invariants_test.go). Five load-bearing differences from a first-story-for-table CRUD vertical (BE-0457 deployments, BE-0463 job_attempts, etc.): (a) NO migration is added because the table already exists -- grep the schema_test.go assertions BEFORE writing to learn the column shape and the CHECK / UNIQUE / FK invariants the raw-SQL tests already pin; (b) the typed repository MUST NOT add columns the table lacks even if a comment in another migration suggests otherwise -- migration 0011_optimistic_versions's preamble claims to cover dokploy_refs 'for parity' but its actual ALTER statements only touch organizations / projects / environments / services, so the DokployRef struct MUST NOT carry a Version field and the repository MUST NOT include version in dokployRefColumns or scan it (the single fastest way to discover this kind of drift is the error-chain unwrap debug pattern: write a one-shot test that prints %T:%s for each `cur.(unwrapper).Unwrap()` layer, which surfaces the underlying *pgconn.PgError with the SQLSTATE 42703 'column X does not exist' message in one round trip); (c) if the table has NO customer-mutable column the typed repository surface is INSERT + GET + LIST + DELETE only -- no Update method, no optimistic-concurrency If-Match path -- and the file header MUST document this as load-bearing so a future reader does not mistake the absence for