red + empty, Delete-happy + unknown + nil-tx, organization-delete-cascade, and a raw-SQL set_updated_at trigger pin (no bump_version trigger exists despite migration 0011's preamble). New helpers introduced (per-file DokployRef-suffix to avoid store_test collisions): rawDokployRefRow, loadDokployRefRowByID, countDokployRefRowsForOrg, mintDokployID, runInsertDokployRefOrFail, dokployRefTxRollbackSentinel. Reused verbatim: seedOrg/seedProject/seedEnvironment/seedService (schema_test.go), newStore (store_test.go). The byte-identical-bystander tenant-isolation gap-fill is the paired BE-0466 story. Forward-applicable to any future first-typed-repository story whose underlying table landed in an early migration and has been carried by raw-SQL schema tests since (a future idempotency_keys repository would inherit the same template, though without the bigint identity PK twist).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000048-20260519-010141.log:990:- Repository CRUD-and-invariants tests for a **TABLE WHOSE *_repository.go AND PRIMARY *_test.go ALREADY EXIST FROM A PRIOR (NON-PRD) SUBSYSTEM STORY** — i.e. the CRUD-and-invariants PRD story is NOT the first story for the table (BE-0461 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/job_repository_invariants_test.go for provisioning_jobs). Structurally distinct from a "first-story-for-table" CRUD-and-invariants vertical (BE-0457 deployments, BE-0455 quota_reservations, etc.) in three load-bearing ways: (a) NO migration is added — the table landed in an earlier migration (0008_provisioning_jobs.up.sql for provisioning_jobs) and is already exercised by worker-subsystem tests; (b) NO existing helpers may be re-introduced — grep for `jobFixture / insertJob / transitionJob` (or the analogous resource fixtures) BEFORE writing and reuse them verbatim; collisions inside `package store_test` are compile errors; (c) the new file is a GAP-FILL pass against the canonical *_repository_invariants_test.go pattern (deployment_repository_invariants_test.go is the closest template), NOT a reimplementation. Mandatory gap-fill checklist (the 7-test shape this file lands): InsertMintsRowShape (byte-equal raw-SQL re-load vs Insert's RETURNING projection across every column, INCLUDING nullable resource-target legs which must round-trip as SQL NULL not empty string), InsertDuplicateIDReturnsConflict (PRIMARY KEY collision with a DIFFERENT idempotency key — distinct from the UNIQUE (organization_id, idempotency_key) violation already pinned), InsertRollbackPersistsNoRow (sentinel-error rollback + countXxxRowsForOrg == 0 after), GetUnknownReturnsNotFound (same-tenant unknown id, NOT the cross-tenant variant — pgx.ErrNoRows must map to typed apierr.NotFound), ListByOrganizationReturnsReverseChronological (explicit sleeps + 3 rows + assert ordered created_at DESC, id DESC), ListByOrganizationEmptyReturnsEmptySlice (pin len == 0 rather than 