heritance resolver) — that story consumes the at-rest seam through Provider.Open against multiple scopes simultaneously and needs its own pattern around the merge order + per-scope Open call site. NOT applicable to BE-0351 (secret encryption key rotation) — that story consumes the partial index organization_variables_secret_routing_idx + the KeyIDs() / ActiveKeyID() surface to enumerate rows referencing a retired key and re-Seal them, but the rotation worker is a separate operational concern from the at-rest write path this pattern owns.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000048-20260519-010141.log:1122:- POST sub-action endpoint on a deep resource by bare id (BE-0163 pattern, POST /v1/environments/{environment_id}/clone, store/environmentservice.go EnvironmentService.Clone + CloneEnvironmentInput + validateCloneEnvironmentInput, httpapi/environments.go cloneEnvironmentHandler + EnvironmentCloner): canonical shape for ALL sub-action POSTs on a bare-id route (clone, restart, rollback, cancel, restore, etc.). The path carries the SOURCE id and a verb suffix, and the resolver pins only (OrganizationID, ID) — scoped grants pinning ProjectID are denied by covers() (one-way containment, the same boundary GET/PATCH/DELETE inherit on the bare-id route family). The structural parent_id of the new row (project_id for env.clone, etc.) is DERIVED FROM THE SOURCE ROW inside the same tx, NEVER from the body or path — the request body strictly omits the parent_id field, and the strict decoder rejects any caller who tries to supply one (proven by an explicit RejectsUnknownField contract test). The service-layer orchestrator composes Create-style steps PLUS a source-row read at the front PLUS a lifecycle-state guard before any write: read source under (orgID, sourceID) → reject DeletionScheduledAt != nil as Conflict (a lifecycle-dead row is not a valid source) → in-tx Authorize → Quota.Reserve → Repository.Insert (the new row inherits source.ProjectID) → JobEnqueue → Audit.Append with Metadata{"slug","project_id","cloned_from": source.ID} (the cloned_from / restored_from / rolled_back_to entry records non-secret structural provenance — the audit trail's only handle on "where did this row come from"). Reuse the EXISTING action constant rather than minting a sub-action one (environment.create on a clone route, not environment.clone): the PRD-mandated action is the same CapWrite, same role matrix, same grant containment, and a new action constant would force a sweep of the action catalog, builtinRoleCaps, every policy matr