./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000048-20260519-010141.log:1163:- Persistence access goes through internal/controlplane/store: Store.Read (read-only tx -> Querier) and Store.Write (read/write tx -> *Tx; commit on nil, rollback on ANY error or panic). A *Tx is obtainable ONLY inside Store.Write; repository mutation methods take *Tx, read methods take Querier — so a mutation structurally cannot run outside the transaction that also carries its authorization and quota checks. A unit of work validates input first, then composes authorize -> reserve quota -> write desired state -> enqueue durable job inside one Store.Write. The policy/quota/jobs dependencies are narrow port interfaces defined IN store (Authorizer, QuotaReserver, JobEnqueuer); store never imports those packages. Error mapping is uniform: pgx.ErrNoRows -> apierr.NotFound, SQLSTATE class 23 -> apierr.Conflict, other driver errors -> apierr.StoreUnavailable; the raw cause is wrapped for logging only. ProjectRepository/ProjectService are the reference implementation.
