./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000010-20260518-165333.log:963:- Repository CRUD invariants for a **multi-table resource FAMILY whose physical realization is one table per scope in the Organization -> Project -> Environment -> Service hierarchy, sharing identical CHECK / FK / CASCADE / bump_version / set_updated_at invariants but with per-scope mutation surfaces** (BE-0449 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/{organization,project,environment,service}_variable_repository_invariants_test.go). A PRD note that reads "Database table: <name>" can refer to such a family (variables = 4 scope tables, quota_* = 3 ledger tables) — when the family is hierarchical, ship one *_repository_invariants_test.go per physical table rather than collapsing into a single mega-file, because per-scope mutation surfaces diverge (organization_variables uniquely exposes UpdateMutable + DeleteByKey on top of the bulk-replace surface; project / environment / service variables expose only the bulk Upsert + DeleteByXxxExceptKeys pair). Each file in the family extends the BE-0447 grant-table invariants template with three uniform substitutions: (a) the Upsert payload struct is the scope's XxxVariableUpsert (Value, IsSecret, SecretProvider, SecretKeyID, SecretCiphertext) instead of role + principal_kind; (b) a brand-new secret_columns_consistent CHECK-violation test is added (IsSecret=true with non-empty Value triggers the secret branch's `value=''` clause and surfaces as typed apierr.Conflict — exhaustively probing the OTHER drift directions is needless because the repository's nullableSecretColumns helper makes them structurally impossible from the caller side); (c) the leaf-scope variants (env / service) add a cross-tenant composite-FK test mirroring BE-0447's service-grant cross-tenant proof. Every *_test.go file under internal/controlplane/store/ shares the same store_test package, so the per-scope helpers MUST get distinct names — newOrganizationVariableID / newEnvironmentVariableID / newServiceVariableID, upsertOrganizationVariable / upsertEnvironmentVariable / upsertServiceVariable, listOrganizationVariablesOrFail / listEnvironmentVariablesOrFail / listServiceVariablesOrFail, and organizationVariableTxRollbackSentinel / projectVariableTxRollbackSentinel / environmentVariableTxRollbackSentinel / serviceVariableTxRollbackSentinel. The project-variables file is the smallest because project_variable_test.go already covers Upsert INSERT/UPDATE happy paths, cross-tenant rejection, the bulk delete surface, and the nil-Tx guards — its invariants file pins ONLY the row-shape and lifecycle invariants the existing tests do not anchor (version=1 default, byte-equal created_at == updated_at, ON CONFLICT id+created_at preservation, PK reuse -> Conflict, secret CHECK violation, ON DELETE CASCADE, Upsert tx-rollback). Forward-applicable to any future multi-table family at this hierarchy (a hypothetical KindOrganizationSetting / KindProjectSetting / KindEnvironmentSetting / KindServiceSetting feature would inherit this 4-file template structure).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000010-20260518-165333.log:964:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **tenant-scoped LEAF-grant table whose ONLY mutation surface is an INSERT...ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE upsert PLUS a bulk DELETE-by-exclusion, with a database-managed version column, NO nullable scope pointer below the parent FK, and a composite FK to a leaf-entity parent (organization_id, service_id) -> services** (BE-0447 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/service_grant_repository_invariants_test.go). Structural reduction of the BE-0443 environment_grant_repository_invariants_test.go template: every leg that exercised a nullable *string scope pointer collapses or drops out — the round-trip pointer test is replaced by a service-account-principal-kind test (the closed-set CHECK leg still needs proving), the NULLS-FIRST ordering assertion in ListByService is gone (two-column ORDER BY principal_id, id), the empty-string-COALESCE dedup equivalence leg is gone (no COALESCE in the unique index), and the upsert/replace input struct drops the trailing *string field. The Upsert signature is six-positional `(id, organization_id, parent_id, principal_id, principal_kind, role)`; the ON CONFLICT branch keys on the three-tuple `(organization_id, parent_id, principal_id)`. The principal-kind cross-smuggling invariant MUST be preserved verbatim (re-upsert with a different caller-supplied principal_kind for the same principal_id; assert persisted kind = baseline). The duplicate-PK test must use a DIFFERENT principal_id so the ON CONFLICT branch does NOT match and the PRIMARY KEY (id) uniqueness violation is exercised instead of the upsert path. The ON DELETE CASCADE proof must delete the parent via raw SQL (the ServiceRepository.ScheduleDeletion is a SOFT delete and would NOT trigger CASCADE). The Upsert rollback proof reduces to ListByService-only because no per-id Get exists; ListByService is the only observation surface for a grant row. NEW Kind constant in domain/id.go MUST be added to BOTH the const block AND the canonical `kinds` map at the bottom — Valid() and the ID parser read from the map, not the const list, so a missing map entry silently breaks NewID(KindFoo) with ErrUnknownKind. For brand-new tables, services already exposes UNIQUE (organization_id, id) from migration 0002 so NO companion ALTER TABLE is needed on the parent (UNLIKE BE-0435 api_keys parent). Forward-applicable to any future grant table whose parent IS the leaf of the Organization -> Project -> Environment -> Service hierarchy or whose parent is otherwise structurally leaf-like (a hypothetical KindDeploymentGrant / KindJobGrant would inherit this template).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000010-20260518-165333.log:965:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **tenant-scoped child table whose ONLY mutation surface is an INSERT...ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE upsert PLUS a bulk DELETE-by-exclusion (no per-id Get, no per-id Delete, no traditional UPDATE), with a database-managed version column, optional nullable scoping pointers, and a composite FK to a parent (organization_id, project_id) -> projects** (BE-0439 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/project_grant_repository_invariants_test.go). Two structural divergences from BE-0435 (api_key_scope_repository_invariants_test.go) are load-bearing: (1) the Upsert ON CONFLICT branch must be tested with a DIFFERENT caller-supplied id AND a DIFFERENT caller-supplied principal_kind to prove BOTH the caller-id-is-ignored guarantee AND the cross-kind-smuggling-impossible guarantee — the principal_kind column is NOT part of the scope tuple, so an existing row stays at its current principal_kind even when the caller passes a different kind for the same principal_id; a single Role-only update test would silently pass while a regression that promoted principal_kind to a SET clause still went undetected. (2) The Upsert rollback proof reduces to ListByProject-only because the repository exposes no per-id Get for grants — ListByProject is the ONLY observation surface for a grant row, so it is the load-bearing leak channel a partial commit would surface through, and an absent Get assertion is a deliberate file boundary, not a gap. Insert duplicate-id test must use a DIFFERENT principal_id so the ON CONFLICT (org, proj, principal, env, svc) branch does NOT match and the PRIMARY KEY (id) uniqueness violation is exercised — otherwise the upsert path silently swallows the duplicate id. DeleteByProjectExceptIDs has TWO codepaths in the repository (len(keepIDs)==0 -> unconditional DELETE; len>0 -> DELETE WHERE id NOT IN (ANY $3::text[])), so BOTH must be exercised independently — the empty-keep tes