./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000010-20260518-165333.log:966:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **tenant-scoped table whose mutation surface spans FOUR distinct UPDATE paths (Update / UpdateDisplayName / ScheduleDeletion / Restore) PLUS Insert, with a database-managed version column AND a nullable soft-delete column (deletion_scheduled_at)** (BE-0437 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/project_repository_invariants_test.go): this is the BE-0425 organization template extended with the second-UPDATE-path projection (UpdateDisplayName must run the dual-anchor AND prove the path-specific WHERE/SET isolation — the row's slug must be untouched since the SET clause is `SET display_name = $3` only) and the BE-0431 inverse-soft-delete projection (Restore must dual-anchor AND clear deletion_scheduled_at back to NULL — the trigger fires on any UPDATE so a forgotten `SET deletion_scheduled_at = NULL` clause would still pass the version/timestamp anchors, making the "deletion_scheduled_at is nil after Restore" assertion the load-bearing one). Insert rollback proof must span ALL read surfaces the rolled-back row touches: by-id Get, by-org ListByOrganization, AND CountByOrganization (the count the quota layer reads), so a future refactor that switched Insert to a SAVEPOINT or autonomous transaction would leak the row into a quota check even though Get reports NotFound. The nil-Tx typed-Internal guard only needs to close the ONE mutation path the existing tests did not cover (here UpdateDisplayName) — duplicating Insert/Update/ScheduleDeletion/Restore guards already proved elsewhere is noise. Test fixtures compose seedOrg + projectFixture(f.Project(org, label)) + insertProject helpers from project_test.go; do not re-implement them at package scope.
