./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000010-20260518-165333.log:1069:- Cross-cutting capability package + at-rest encryption seam (BE-0339 pattern, internal/controlplane/secrets/{doc.go, provider.go, aesgcm.go, plaintext.go, *_test.go, AGENTS.md} + internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/0029_organization_variables_encrypted_secrets.{up,down}.sql + internal/controlplane/store/organization_variable.go + organization_variable_service.go + organization_variable_secrets_at_rest_test.go + cmd/yalla-api/main.go buildSecretsProvider; structural template for BE-0340..0342 sibling at-rest stories (project / environment / service variable encryption-at-rest) and any future cross-cutting source-of-truth seam over a same-shape resource family — webhook signing secrets, deployment-config secrets, backup-target credentials, etc.). Six load-bearing rules for the cross-cutting package: (1) Land the package ONCE under internal/controlplane/<pkg>, with the Provider interface + a production implementation (AESGCM) + a tests-only passthrough implementation (Plaintext, restricted to local/test profiles by cmd/yalla-api) + a package AGENTS.md that documents BOTH the runtime contract AND the forward-applicable storage pattern (column shape, CHECK constraint shape, repository tuple shape, service-layer seam location). (2) Typed value-free errors (ErrInvalidCiphertext / ErrUnknownKey / ErrUnsupportedProvider) — the secrets package contract never echoes any of {plaintext, ciphertext bytes, key material, key id, nonce} into an error message; the only observable on a failure is the classification. (3) AES-256-GCM with per-Seal random crypto/rand nonce + AEAD-authenticated decryption + multi-key rotation pool (first key is active for Seal, all keys accepted for Open). KeyID derivation = first 8 bytes of SHA-256(key) hex-encoded (16 chars): deterministic across processes, non-secret (one-way hash), short enough for audit metadata. NewAESGCM rejects duplicate keys at construction so a misconfigu