./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000075-20260519-041333.log:9639:- Repository CRUD invariants for a **multi-table resource FAMILY whose physical realization is one table per scope in the Organization -> Project -> Environment -> Service hierarchy, sharing identical CHECK / FK / CASCADE / bump_version / set_updated_at invariants but with per-scope mutation surfaces** (BE-0449 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/{organization,project,environment,service}_variable_repository_invariants_test.go). A PRD note that reads "Database table: <name>" can refer to such a family (variables = 4 scope tables, quota_* = 3 ledger tables) — when the family is hierarchical, ship one *_repository_invariants_test.go per physical table rather than collapsing into a single mega-file, because per-scope mutation surfaces diverge (organization_variables uniquely exposes UpdateMutable + DeleteByKey on top of the bulk-replace surface; project / environment / service variables expose only the bulk Upsert + DeleteByXxxExceptKeys pair). Each file in the family extends the BE-0447 grant-table invariants template with three uniform substitutions: (a) the Upsert payload struct is the scope's XxxVariableUpsert (Value, IsSecret, SecretProvider, SecretKeyID, SecretCiphertext) instead of role + principal_kind; (b) a brand-new secret_columns_consistent CHECK-violation test is added (IsSecret=true with non-empty Value triggers the secret branch's `value=''` clause and surfaces as typed apierr.Conflict — exhaustively probing the OTHER drift directions is needless because the repository's nullableSecretColumns helper makes them structurally impossible from the caller side); (c) the leaf-scope variants (env / service) add a cross-tenant composite-FK test mirroring BE-0447's service-grant cross-tenant proof. Every *_test.go file under internal/controlplane/store/ shares the same store_test package, so the per-scope helpers MUST get distinct names — newOrganizationVariableID / newEnvironmentVariableID / newServi