*time.Time fields so pending NULLs are distinguishable from zero-value scalars), loadIdempotencyRowByID, countIdempotencyRowsForOrg, mintIdempotencyID, idempotencyTxRollbackSentinel. REUSED verbatim from sibling idempotency_test.go: idemFixture, claimIdem, completeIdem, findIdem, wantErrCode, newIdempotencyStore; from schema_test.go: seedOrg; from store_test.go: newStore. NO migration added. The byte-identical-bystander tenant-isolation gap-fill is the paired BE-0470 story. Forward-applicable to any future PRD CRUD-and-invariants story whose underlying table has a claim-protocol-style upsert on a non-PK UNIQUE tuple with a multi-column completion-consistent CHECK (e.g. a future webhook-delivery-claims or rate-limit-burst-tokens table).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000077-20260519-042229.log:1020:- Repository CRUD-and-invariants tests for a **TABLE WHOSE SCHEMA ALREADY EXISTS FROM AN EARLY MIGRATION BUT WHOSE TYPED REPOSITORY IS THE FIRST STORY-LEVEL CALLER** -- i.e. the table landed in an ancient migration (dokploy_refs in 0002_tenant_hierarchy) and has been exercised only by raw-SQL schema_test.go tests; the CRUD-and-invariants PRD story creates BOTH the *_repository.go file AND the *_repository_invariants_test.go file from scratch (BE-0465 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/dokploy_ref.go + internal/controlplane/store/dokploy_ref_repository_invariants_test.go). Five load-bearing differences from a first-story-for-table CRUD vertical (BE-0457 deployments, BE-0463 job_attempts, etc.): (a) NO migration is added because the table already exists -- grep the schema_test.go assertions BEFORE writing to learn the column shape and the CHECK / UNIQUE / FK invariants the raw-SQL tests already pin; (b) the typed repository MUST NOT add columns the table lacks even if a comment in another migration suggests otherwise -- migration 0011_optimistic_versions's preamble claims to cover dokploy_refs 'for parity' but its actual ALTER statements only touch organizations / projects / environments / services, so the DokployRef struct MUST NOT carry a Version field and the repository MUST NOT include version in dokployRefColumns or scan it (the single fastest way to discover this kind of drift is the error-chain unwrap debug pattern: write a one-shot test that prints %T:%s for each `cur.(unwrapper).Unwrap()` layer, which surfaces the underlying *pgconn.PgError with the SQLSTATE 42703 'column X does not exist' message in one round trip); (c) if the table has NO customer-mutable column the typed repository surface is INSERT + GET + LIST + DELETE only -- no Update method, no optimistic-concurrency If-Match path -- and the file header MUST document this as load-bearing so a future reader does not mistake the absence for a coverage gap (the 'optimistic versioning where applicable' acceptance-criteria phrase narrows to 'not applicable here'); (d) when the table has a bigint GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY (the FIRST and ONLY int64 PK in the store package), the typed struct's ID field is int64 (not string), the INSERT statement OMITS id from the column list entirely (any value supplied -- even NULL or DEFAULT -- trips SQLSTATE 428C9 'cannot insert a non-DEFAULT value into column "id"'), and the typed error payload renders the int64 id via a private package-local helper rather than importing strconv -- keeping the store package's 'no strconv' invariant intact. A test InsertIgnoresCallerSuppliedID is the regression backstop (a caller that smuggles ID: 999_999_999 must still see the database-minted id in the returned struct); (e) when the table has TWO UNIQUE constraints, one GLOBAL across tenants (e.g. (dokploy_resource, dokploy_id) on dokploy_refs -- a Dokploy object cannot be claimed twice across tenants) and one PER-TENANT (e.g. (organization_id, yalla_id, dokploy_resource, dokploy_id)), BOTH must be exercised explicitly by the invariants tests -- the global-UNIQUE test must seed orgA's row then try to insert orgB's row with the SAME (dokploy_resource, dokploy_id) and assert countRowsForOrg(orgB) == 0 after the rejection. The 19-test shape this file lands: Insert-row-shape (raw-SQL byte-equal), Insert-ignores-caller-supplied-id, four typed-Internal rejections (nil-tx + blank-closed-set-args), four CHECK/FK-violation Conflicts (unknown-yalla_kind, unknown-dokploy_resource, blank-yalla_id, blank-dokploy_id, unknown-organization_id), both UNIQUE violations (global + per-tenant), positive-direction 'multiple domains for same service all persist' (pins the per-tenant UNIQUE includes dokploy_id), Insert-rollback, Get-happy + Get-unknown, GetByDokployTarget-happy + unknown + blank-resource-Internal, ListByYallaResource-ordered + empty + blank-kind-Internal, ListByOrganization-ord