wShape (a fresh Claim must leave all three completion columns NULL); the completed-side by TestIdempotencyRepositoryCompleteRowShape (after Complete, all three must be non-NULL AND a raw-SQL re-load must byte-equal the returned struct, AND created_at + expires_at must NOT have drifted across the Complete UPDATE -- only the four completion columns transition). (c) The Complete method's `now time.Time` argument is the only application-controlled timestamp on the table: created_at + expires_at are caller-supplied via Claim and completed_at can be caller-supplied via Complete's now arg (zero defaults to time.Now().UTC()). TestIdempotencyRepositoryCompleteHonoursExplicitNow uses a specific 2024 timestamp far from time.Now() so a regression that ignored the arg and wrote time.Now() would fail with an obvious delta. This is a structurally distinct invariant from BE-0467 (audit_events) where ALL timestamps are server-side via DEFAULT now() and a caller-supplied OccurredAt must be discarded. (d) The id minter newIdempotencyID emits `idk_<32hex>` (16 bytes of crypto/rand entropy hex-encoded — 4 + 32 = 36 chars total). The row-shape probe MUST pin BOTH the prefix AND the total length so a regression that shortened the entropy or reformatted the prefix surfaces here. Test-local mintIdempotencyID(t, suffix) follows the established per-file suffixed-helper pattern (`idk_`+t.Name()+`_`+suffix) so parallel tests that need a deterministic caller-supplied id (to force a PK collision) cannot collide. (e) The Release method has NO pre-validation coverage in the primary idempotency_test.go's TestIdempotencyClaimValidation (which only covers Claim nil-tx + Claim missing-fields + Complete nil-tx + Complete out-of-range-status). The invariants file fills the Release gap with TestIdempotencyRepositoryReleaseRejectsNilTx so all three mutating methods (Claim / Complete / Release) have a pinned nil-tx guard. The 15-test shape this file lands: Claim-row-shape (raw-SQL byte-equal + idk_ prefix +