./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000161-20260519-170137.log:1437:- Repository tenant-isolation test file for a **tenant-scoped row whose mutation surface spans FIVE distinct methods (UpdateMutable / Revoke / RotateCredential / TouchLastUsed plus the Insert path) AND whose row body carries TWO load-bearing credential primitives (a globally-UNIQUE prefix and a secret-bearing secret_hash)** (BE-0434 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/api_key_tenant_isolation_test.go; the cross-tenant analogue of BE-0433 and the secret-bearing variant of the BE-0432 service_accounts shape). Two schema-level facts make this pattern structurally distinct from BE-0432: (i) api_keys.prefix is GLOBALLY UNIQUE (NOT UNIQUE (organization_id, prefix) — the prefix authentication lookup runs BEFORE the caller's tenant is known) so the BE-0432 "two tenants share a slug" worst-case fixture has no row-level analogue here; the cross-tenant prefix-conflict path is still load-bearing (orgA Insert with orgB's already-persisted prefix AND orgA RotateCredential to orgB's prefix) and BOTH paths must surface CodeConflict, leave orgB's bystander row byte-identical, and leave NO row anywhere carrying the rolled-back secret_hash needle (raw-SQL probe). (ii) api_keys carries a secret-bearing column — secret_hash — so the cross-tenant byte-identical-bystander assertion includes a `assertRawSecretHashUnchanged` raw-SQL probe AGAINST the typed-read SecretHash field (the typed read path is already covered by the struct snapshot, but a regression that scanned a non-secret column into the struct or skipped the field on Get would silently pass the struct check while the underlying row drifted — the raw probe is the load-bearing safety net for THAT class of regression specifically), and the cross-tenant indistinguishability test additionally asserts the secret_hash needle does NOT appear in any of the typed-error surfaces yeCross.Error() / yeCross.Message / yeCross.Hint across ALL five mutation methods (the secret-bearing redaction probe extension to the BE-0432 Code+Hint indistinguishability rule). Skeleton: one t.Parallel test per (mutation × leg) plus a 5-row indistinguishability-and-redaction table test that iterates (Get, UpdateMutable, Revoke, RotateCredential, TouchLastUsed). Three load-bearing rules: (1) Every byte-identical-bystander test asserts BOTH the trigger-managed updated_at (the api_keys_set_updated_at BEFORE-UPDATE trigger refreshes it on every matched UPDATE, including a WHERE-on-id-only UPDATE that touched the wrong tenant) AND the lifecycle column the OWNING method writes (revoked_at for Revoke, last_used_at for TouchLastUsed, prefix+secret_hash for RotateCredential, name+scopes for UpdateMutable) so a WHERE-on-id-only regression surfaces independently on EITHER anchor. (2) The Insert cross-tenant prefix-conflict test must add a SELECT COUNT(*) FROM api_keys global-table-size probe AFTER the conflicting Insert — a rolled-back Insert that landed its row in some OTHER tenant's slot would show up there even if the per-id probe missed it; the per-id probe alone is insufficient because the failing row's id is not known to the probe. (3) FindByPrefix is INTENTIONALLY NOT a cross-tenant probe surface — the signature carries no caller-tenant parameter, the prefix column is globally unique, and the resolved row carries its own organization_id; document this absence in the test file's package-doc comment so a future reader does not look for a missing test (mirrors BE-0426's "tenant-root tables have no ListByParent" note). Helper shape worth pinning forward: a `getXOrFail(ctx, t, s, repo, orgID, id, label) X` and a `writeX(ctx, s, fn) (X, error)` pair keep byte-identical snapshot tests free of Read/Write closure boilerplate; combined with a single `assertBystanderByteIdentical(t, label, baseline, after)` helper they reduce a 12-column equality check to two lines per (mutation × leg). Forward-applicable to BE-0436 (api_key_scopes tenant isolation — a child-table variant with NO secret-bearing column and only one mutation surface, so the secret-bearing redaction probe and most of the conflict-rollback shape collapse; the LIST-by-parent isolation rule remains) and to BE-0450 (variables tenant isolation, where the secret-bearing column is value WHEN is_secret=true, so the rolled-back-secret probe rule applies CONDITIONALLY on is_secret — the same shape extended with a per-row classification check). Use docker compose up -d postgres + YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestAPIKeyRepository.*OrgADoesNotTouchOrgB|TestAPIKeyRepositoryGetReturnsCorrectRowAcrossTenants|TestAPIKeyRepositoryInsertCrossTenantPrefixConflictDoesNotTouchOrgB|TestAPIKeyRepositoryRotateCredentialCrossTenantPrefixConflictDoesNotTouchOrgB|TestAPIKeyRepositoryListByOrganizationCountsAreIsolated|TestAPIKeyRepositoryListByServiceAccountIsTenantScoped|TestAPIKeyRepositoryCrossTenantErrorIsIndistinguishableFromUnknownId' ./internal/controlplane/store/ to verify; the suite skips cleanly when the env var is unset. Same pre-existing -race-with-DB unrelated regressions noted under BE-0426/BE-0432 still apply — confirmed by stashing the new file and re-running, the failing tests are environment-service / api-key-service Create paths, organization_variable_patch audit metadata, and TestSQLArgsAreConstantExpressions; none are touched by this pattern.
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000161-20260519-170137.log:1446:- PUT-contract four-test shape for /v1/<scope>/variables endpoints (BE-0146 pattern, internal/controlplane/httpapi/project_variables_put_contract_test.go): four tests — (1) server writes response data only through http.ResponseWriter (captureProcessOutput, NOT t.Parallel), (2) bearer-credential redaction in log buffer AND response body on BOTH success and deny legs (disabled-principal deny + err-on-call replacer to prove deny path is not the leak source), (3) submitted is_secret=true value redaction in log buffer AND response body on BOTH legs (the variables-WRITE-specific extra surface vs the read-only sibling), (4) dependency-cause leak pin including bare datastore address (apierr.StoreUnavailable wraps a "connection refused dialing 10.0.0.5:5432" cause; the typed 503 envelope must carry a stable generic message). The fourth test is the differentiator from the BE-0140 / BE-0143 read-only contract shape, which only needs three tests. The deny-leg redaction pin in test #3 is load-bearing: the deny path is precisely where a future regression that dumps the decoded body is most dangerous (the secret never reached the store but still reaches the operator log). Helper pattern: one replaceXxxHandlerForWithLogger that mirrors the existing replaceXxxHandlerFor with the final two NewHandler positional args swapped from (nil, nil) to (logger, nil). Constant pattern: three module-scope constants per file (bearer credential with endpoint-specific hex suffix, submitted secret marker with endpoint-specific hex suffix, canonical replace body that carries both a non-secret and a secret variable). Forward-applicable to every BE-0149..BE-0200 PUT-contract story whose request body can carry is_secret=true items.
