ith NO secret-bearing column and only one mutation surface, so the secret-bearing redaction probe and most of the conflict-rollback shape collapse; the LIST-by-parent isolation rule remains) and to BE-0450 (variables tenant isolation, where the secret-bearing column is value WHEN is_secret=true, so the rolled-back-secret probe rule applies CONDITIONALLY on is_secret — the same shape extended with a per-row classification check). Use docker compose up -d postgres + YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestAPIKeyRepository.*OrgADoesNotTouchOrgB|TestAPIKeyRepositoryGetReturnsCorrectRowAcrossTenants|TestAPIKeyRepositoryInsertCrossTenantPrefixConflictDoesNotTouchOrgB|TestAPIKeyRepositoryRotateCredentialCrossTenantPrefixConflictDoesNotTouchOrgB|TestAPIKeyRepositoryListByOrganizationCountsAreIsolated|TestAPIKeyRepositoryListByServiceAccountIsTenantScoped|TestAPIKeyRepositoryCrossTenantErrorIsIndistinguishableFromUnknownId' ./internal/controlplane/store/ to verify; the suite skips cleanly when the env var is unset. Same pre-existing -race-with-DB unrelated regressions noted under BE-0426/BE-0432 still apply — confirmed by stashing the new file and re-running, the failing tests are environment-service / api-key-service Create paths, organization_variable_patch audit metadata, and TestSQLArgsAreConstantExpressions; none are touched by this pattern.
