must be proven independently; a regression that dropped the organization_id leg of either FK would surface as either a bravo row vanishing or its byte content drifting. (d) The "soft-deleted rows where applicable" acceptance-criteria phrase narrows to "where applicable": deployment_events has no soft-delete column and no Delete repository surface, so cascade is the analogous proof and is the substitute test surface — the file header MUST document this delegation explicitly so a future reader does not mistake the absence for a coverage gap. (e) The metadata column is jsonb stored as []byte; bystander byte-identity uses bytes.Equal not json equivalence (a regression that stripped or reordered keys would defeat json equivalence but survive bytes.Equal — and the test wants to catch ANY rewrite, semantic or representational). The 8-test shape (Append-bystander-byte-identity across queued+running+progress peers / Append-row-count-invariant / Append-foreign-parent-deployment-rejected-BOTH-directions-with-forged-id-not-persisted+bystander-byte-identity / GetByID-cross-tenant-NotFound-with-no-leak (message/metadata key/value/request_id/correlation_id/event_type/deployment_id) / ListByDeployment-cross-tenant-empty-and-counts-unchanged across per-org AND per-deployment probes / ListByDeployment-foreign-deployment-id-of-SAME-tenant-returns-empty (composite (organization_id, deployment_id) probe distinct from "foreign org+foreign deployment") / parent-deployment-delete-cascade-is-tenant-scoped across queued+running+progress orgB peers / parent-organization-delete-cascade-is-tenant-scoped) leaves BE-0459's invariants surface (CRUD/append-only-trigger/closed-set-event_type/composite-FK/duplicate-id/nil-tx/rollback/metadata-redaction/caller-supplied-occurred_at/cascade-on-deployment) untouched. Helpers reused from BE-0459: rawDeploymentEventRow, loadDeploymentEventRowByID, countDeploymentEventRowsForDeployment, mintDeploymentEventID, runAppendDeploymentEventOrFail, seedDeploymentEvent; from BE-0458: seedTwoTenantDeploymentFixture, twoTenantDeploymentFixture type; from BE-0457: seedQueuedDeployment; from store_test: seedOrg/seedProject/seedEnvironment/seedService, newStore, containsValue. New helpers introduced (unique to this file): twoTenantDeploymentEventFixture + seedTwoTenantDeploymentEventFixture (the two-tenant boilerplate that ALSO seeds one parent deployment per tenant, because events need a parent deployment as the FK target — a pure two-tenant org/proj/env/svc fixture is insufficient for events), assertDeploymentEventByteIdentical (anchored on every column INCLUDING metadata []byte via bytes.Equal; NO version/updated_at columns to anchor cross-row UPDATE detection), countDeploymentEventRowsForOrg (per-tenant aggregate variant of countDeploymentEventRowsForDeployment — the cascade tests need both, per-tenant is the cascade-scoped probe, per-deployment is the Append-scoped probe). Forward-applicable to any tenant-isolation story whose table is an append-only child anchored by a composite FK to a tenant-scoped parent with cascade (e.g. future audit_events / job_events / log lines stories).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000118-20260519-094450.log:1054:- Repository tenant-isolation tests for a **TENANT-SCOPED LIFECYCLE-BEARING table whose Insert is caller-id, whose state-transition surface is a single Cancel() with optimistic-concurrency disambiguation, whose row body carries a lifecycle CHECK and a bump_version + set_updated_at trigger pair, AND whose global PRIMARY KEY (id) makes deployment ids strictly per-tenant-distinct even though every OTHER per-row anchor (UNIQUE (organization_id, idempotency_key), source_ref, source/status taxonomies) is per-tenant** (BE-0458 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/deployment_tenant_isolation_test.go). Structurally distinct from BE-0456 (quota_reservations — INSERT-only mutation surface, no Cancel, the row body has nullable string columns) in five load-bearing ways: (a) the bystander byte-identity assertion is anchored on TWO trigger-managed columns simultaneously — set_updated_at refreshes updated_at on any matched UPDATE AND the bump_version trigger increments version on the same UPDATE — so a regression that swept a peer tenant's row through a missing organization_id predicate surfaces as either an updated_at drift OR a version bump, not just one. (b) The Insert positive-direction pair is "same-(idempotency_key, source_ref) in two tenants both persist" instead of "same-resource in two tenants both persist", because the only per-tenant UNIQUE on this table is (organization_id, idempotency_key); the test must also assert FindByIdempotencyKey resolves the SAME key to the per-tenant row never cross-tenant — this is the read-side proof of the positive-direction shape. (c) The cross-tenant Cancel probe MUST seed BOTH a target row and an UNRELATED sibling for the same orgA, then byte-identity-assert BOTH after orgB's Cancel — without the sibling, a regression that widened the predicate by status alone (status IN ('queued','running')) would touch every queued row across both tenants and the target-only assertion would