./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000118-20260519-094450.log:1055:- Repository CRUD-and-invariants tests for a **TENANT-SCOPED LIFECYCLE-BEARING table whose Insert is caller-id (no per-row id minting in the repository), whose only public state-transition surface is a single Cancel() with optimistic-concurrency disambiguation, and whose row body carries a lifecycle CHECK (terminal-status <-> finished_at) plus a bump_version trigger** (BE-0457 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/deployment_repository_invariants_test.go). Structurally distinct from BE-0455 (quota_reservations — the repository mints qres_<token> ids and has no Update/Cancel surface) in three load-bearing ways: (a) the test must mint deployment ids itself (DeploymentService.Create owns domain.NewID(domain.KindDeployment); the repo does NOT mint). A test-local mintDeploymentID(t, suffix) helper using `"dep_"+t.Name()+"_"+suffix` avoids global PK collisions across parallel cases without a shared atomic counter — every *_test.go under internal/controlplane/store/ shares one package, so t.Name() is the natural disambiguator. (b) The terminal-status-on-Insert probe leverages the deployments_finished_consistent CHECK: Insert's INSERT column list omits finished_at, so any terminal Status passed in violates the CHECK by construction (status terminal AND finished_at NULL). This is the one-line proof that this surface can only mint non-terminal rows; no separate trigger test is needed. (c) Cancel exercises THREE disambiguation legs against the SAME *Tx — nil expectedVersion + terminal row -> apierr.Conflict (no current_version attached), non-nil expectedVersion + version mismatch -> apierr.ConflictStale (current_version attached, verified via apierr.CurrentVersionOf), unknown id -> apierr.NotFound. The cross-tenant Cancel probe MUST include a byte-identity assertion on the foreign-tenant row (status unchanged, finished_at still NULL, version not bumped) — without it, a regression that scoped the UPDATE by id alone a