./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000118-20260519-094450.log:1057:- Repository CRUD invariants test file for a **TENANT-SCOPED COUNTER table whose ONLY public mutation surface is an INSERT...ON CONFLICT (organization_id, resource) DO NOTHING + SELECT...FOR UPDATE primitive (LockUsage), with NO per-row Update/Delete, NO version column, NO service_id pointer, and a database-managed used_value mutated by an EXTERNAL code path (quota.Checker, not the repository), set_updated_at trigger fires BEFORE UPDATE only** (BE-0453 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/quota_usage_repository_invariants_test.go). Structurally distinct from BE-0451 (quota_policies — INSERT...ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE upsert) in four load-bearing ways: (a) the second-call byte-identity proof must anchor updated_at TOO — ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING is not an UPDATE and the set_updated_at trigger must not fire (a regression that switched to ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE with even a no-op SET would silently bump updated_at and a missing anchor would let that slip past); (b) the peer-row proof is a SAME-TENANT-DIFFERENT-RESOURCE check (UNIQUE (organization_id, resource) isolates rows by resource within a tenant); (c) the row-already-exists-with-non-zero-value leg has no policies analog — pre-seed via raw SQL at a sentinel value (e.g. used_value=17, id=`qu_seed_<resource>`) and prove BOTH the seeded id AND the seeded used_value survive a LockUsage call (this is the ONLY way to prove the discarded INSERT's minted prefix id does not replace the row's id — a regression to ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET id=EXCLUDED.id would be a catastrophic data-loss path that typed reader projections would not catch); (d) the DOMAIN-violation test casts an arbitrary string to the typed Resource (e.g. `store.QuotaResource("not-a-resource")`) to bypass Go's compile-time check and exercise the DOMAIN quota_resource CHECK at the database layer — surfacing as yerr.CodeConflict through mapWriteError. The 8-new-test shape (row-shape, second-call-byte-identity, peer-row-byte-identity, persisted-used-value, unknown-org-Conflict, unknown-resource-Conflict, tx-rollback, nil-tx-Internal) leaves the pre-existing TestQuotaRepositoryLockUsageCreatesAndReturnsCounter in quota_repository_test.go alone as the load-bearing two-call-idempotency probe. Helper symbols introduced: `lockUsageOrFail`, `loadQuotaUsageRow`, `countQuotaUsageRowsForOrg`, `rawQuotaUsageRow`, `quotaUsageTxRollbackSentinel`. Reused symbols from sibling files: `seedOrg` (schema_test.go), `seedQuotaUsage` (usage_test.go), `newStore` (store_test.go) — note `seedQuotaUsage` is the ONLY way to set used_value to a non-zero value through a test fixture because the repository surface has no equivalent (LockUsage cannot increment).
./ralph/codex-output/iteration-000118-20260519-094450.log:1060:- Repository CRUD invariants for a **multi-table resource FAMILY whose physical realization is one table per scope in the Organization -> Project -> Environment -> Service hierarchy, sharing identical CHECK / FK / CASCADE / bump_version / set_updated_at invariants but with per-scope mutation surfaces** (BE-0449 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/{organization,project,environment,service}_variable_repository_invariants_test.go). A PRD note that reads "Database table: <name>" can refer to such a family (variables = 4 scope tables, quota_* = 3 ledger tables) — when the family is hierarchical, ship one *_repository_invariants_test.go per physical table rather than collapsing into a single mega-file, because per-scope mutation surfaces diverge (organization_variables uniquely exposes UpdateMutable + DeleteByKey on top of the bulk-replace surface; project / environment / service variables expose only the bulk Upsert + DeleteByXxxExceptKeys pair). Each file in the family extends the BE-0447 grant-table invariants template with three uniform substitutions: (a) the Upsert payload struct is the scope's XxxVariableUpsert (Value, IsSecret, SecretProvider, SecretKeyID, SecretCiphertext) instead of role + principal_kind; (b) a brand-new secret_columns_consistent CHECK-violation test is added (IsSecret=true with non-empty Value triggers the secret branch's `value=''` clause and surfaces as typed apierr.Conflict — exhaustively probing the OTHER drift directions is needless because the repository's nullableSecretColumns helper makes them structurally impossible from the caller side); (c) the leaf-scope variants (env / service) add a cross-tenant composite-FK test mirroring BE-0447's service-grant cross-tenant proof. Every *_test.go file under internal/controlplane/store/ shares the same store_test package, so the per-scope helpers MUST get distinct names — newOrganizationVariableID / newEnvironmentVariableID / newServiceVariableID, upsertOrganizationVariable / upsertEnvironmentVariable / upsertServiceVariable, listOrganizationVariablesOrFail / listEnvironmentVariablesOrFail / listServiceVariablesOrFail, and organizationVariableTxRollbackSentinel / projectVariableTxRollbackSentinel / environmentVariableTxRollbackSentinel / serviceVariableTxRollbackSentinel. The project-variables file is the smallest because project_variable_test.go already covers Upsert INSERT/UPDATE happy paths, cross-tenant rejection, the bulk delete surface, and the nil-Tx guards — its invariants file pins ONLY the row-shape and lifecycle invariants the existing tests do not anchor (version=1 default, byte-equal created_at == updated_at, ON CONFLICT id+created_at preservation, PK reuse -> Conflict, secret CHECK violation, ON DELETE CASCADE, Upsert tx-rollback). Forward-applicable to any future multi-table family at this hierarchy (a hypothetical KindOrganizationSetting / KindProjectSetting / KindEnvironmentSetting / KindServiceSetting feature would inherit this 4-file template structure).
