ng redaction probe extension to the BE-0432 Code+Hint indistinguishability rule). Skeleton: one t.Parallel test per (mutation × leg) plus a 5-row indistinguishability-and-redaction table test that iterates (Get, UpdateMutable, Revoke, RotateCredential, TouchLastUsed). Three load-bearing rules: (1) Every byte-identical-bystander test asserts BOTH the trigger-managed updated_at (the api_keys_set_updated_at BEFORE-UPDATE trigger refreshes it on every matched UPDATE, including a WHERE-on-id-only UPDATE that touched the wrong tenant) AND the lifecycle column the OWNING method writes (revoked_at for Revoke, last_used_at for TouchLastUsed, prefix+secret_hash for RotateCredential, name+scopes for UpdateMutable) so a WHERE-on-id-only regression surfaces independently on EITHER anchor. (2) The Insert cross-tenant prefix-conflict test must add a SELECT COUNT(*) FROM api_keys global-table-size probe AFTER the conflicting Insert — a rolled-back Insert that landed its row in some OTHER tenant's slot would show up there even if the per-id probe missed it; the per-id probe alone is insufficient because the failing row's id is not known to the probe. (3) FindByPrefix is INTENTIONALLY NOT a cross-tenant probe surface — the signature carries no caller-tenant parameter, the prefix column is globally unique, and the resolved row carries its own organization_id; document this absence in the test file's package-doc comment so a future reader does not look for a missing test (mirrors BE-0426's "tenant-root tables have no ListByParent" note). Helper shape worth pinning forward: a `getXOrFail(ctx, t, s, repo, orgID, id, label) X` and a `writeX(ctx, s, fn) (X, error)` pair keep byte-identical snapshot tests free of Read/Write closure boilerplate; combined with a single `assertBystanderByteIdentical(t, label, baseline, after)` helper they reduce a 12-column equality check to two lines per (mutation × leg). Forward-applicable to BE-0436 (api_key_scopes tenant isolation — a child-table variant with NO secret-bearing column and only one mutation surface, so the secret-bearing redaction probe and most of the conflict-rollback shape collapse; the LIST-by-parent isolation rule remains) and to BE-0450 (variables tenant isolation, where the secret-bearing column is value WHEN is_secret=true, so the rolled-back-secret probe rule applies CONDITIONALLY on is_secret — the same shape extended with a per-row classification check). Use docker compose up -d postgres + YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://yalla:yalla@127.0.0.1:5432/yalla go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestAPIKeyRepository.*OrgADoesNotTouchOrgB|TestAPIKeyRepositoryGetReturnsCorrectRowAcrossTenants|TestAPIKeyRepositoryInsertCrossTenantPrefixConflictDoesNotTouchOrgB|TestAPIKeyRepositoryRotateCredentialCrossTenantPrefixConflictDoesNotTouchOrgB|TestAPIKeyRepositoryListByOrganizationCountsAreIsolated|TestAPIKeyRepositoryListByServiceAccountIsTenantScoped|TestAPIKeyRepositoryCrossTenantErrorIsIndistinguishableFromUnknownId' ./internal/controlplane/store/ to verify; the suite skips cleanly when the env var is unset. Same pre-existing -race-with-DB unrelated regressions noted under BE-0426/BE-0432 still apply — confirmed by stashing the new file and re-running, the failing tests are environment-service / api-key-service Create paths, organization_variable_patch audit metadata, and TestSQLArgsAreConstantExpressions; none are touched by this pattern.
