 - Security-verification package-confinement pattern, backup-encryption instance (BE-0362 pattern, internal/release/backup_encryption_static_test.go + internal/controlplane/backup/encryption_isolation_test.go + SECURITY.md "## Backup Encryption" section + SECURITY.md Required Verification Gates table row + internal/controlplane/backup/AGENTS.md "Backup encryption boundary (BE-0362)" subsection; EIGHTH worked instance of the BE-0344 two-test template and FIRST whole-package-confinement instance — confirms the template scales from "this single function MUST honour rule X" (BE-0346), "this directory MUST NOT import surface Y" (BE-0357 admin endpoints, BE-0349 SSRF), and "this cross-package secret MUST flow through one seam" (BE-0361 Dokploy token) to "this leaf package MUST NOT carry an entire data plane". Eight load-bearing rules: (1) IMPORT-WHITELIST-AS-FORBIDDEN-LIST — the backup package's only legitimate I/O is os.ReadFile on the operator-supplied status path, so the gate enumerates the symmetric/asymmetric cipher set (crypto/aes, crypto/cipher, crypto/des, crypto/rc4, crypto/rsa, crypto/ecdsa, crypto/ed25519, crypto/tls), the archive/compression set (archive/zip, archive/tar, compress/gzip, compress/zlib, compress/flate, compress/bzip2), the database driver set (database/sql, github.com/jackc/pgx/v5, github.com/jackc/pgx/v5/pgxpool), and the process-boundary set (os/exec, net/http) as a closed forbidden map. The set is intentionally aggressive because the boundary contract is "no data plane", not "this specific library is bad"; a future contributor who needs one of these libraries must surface the design change in review, not slip it in. (2) INTERFACE-METHOD-COUNT-AND-NAMES — the read-only Reporter interface is pinned by name AND by its single method's name (Status). The matcher locates the InterfaceType named Reporter, rejects every field in iface.Methods.List whose len(Names)==0 (embedded interfaces would let any method through, e.g. embed io.Writer would silent